Words for the two end groups
===========================

Status: a checked certificate design, not an implementation or a case result.
No Original marking has been evaluated with this method. The current F004
counts remain unchanged. The ordinary group argument below is not claimed
as a new theorem; the proposed contribution is its use as a small certificate
for the remaining intersection checks.

Let the actual involutions be r0,r1,r2,r3. Set

    L=<r0,r1,r2>, R=<r1,r2,r3>, D=<r1,r2>.

A whole matrix w in L and R but outside D disproves the rank four
intersection property. Complete recognition of L or R is unnecessary.
Schreier calculations may discover the words, but the final consumer only
needs to check the words themselves.

For either end, denote its three actual generators by g0,g1,g2. Start with
T0=V0=I. A lift node (p,j), with strictly earlier p and j in {0,1,2}, defines
Ti=Tp*gj and Vi=gj*Vp. Induction gives Vi=Ti^-1, since gj is an involution.
A recipe (i,j,t) defines He=Ti*gj*Vt. This is an end group word for every
valid i,j,t; t need not describe a genuine orbit edge. Finally, S0=I and
earlier nodes (p,e) define Ss=Sp*He. Choose one S on each side and compare
all 49 matrix entries. Equal matrices give membership in both end groups.

Set a=r1*r2. Check that its first positive identity return is the supplied
bounded integer d. Compare w against all a^i and a^i*r1 for 0<=i<d.
The involution relations show these exhaust D. Only a complete enumeration
and all negative comparisons establish w outside D. Any resource stop or
nonclosing order claim gives no disposition.

One proposed binary format has an eight byte magic, u16 d and, for each
side, u16 n and u8 m,k,w_index. There are n-1 lift entries (u16 parent,
u8 label), k recipes (u16 edge_id,u16 target), and m-1 S entries
(u8 parent,u8 recipe). Here divmod(edge_id,3) gives (i,j). Require exact
EOF, 1<=n<=10000, 1<=m<=128, 0<=k<=8, and m=1 if k=0. The entire
payload is at most 60,586 bytes.

The two word evaluations require at most 40,282 matrix products. Including
the retained Original reconstruction and complete D enumeration gives
40,326+2d products; d<=4096 gives 48,518, below the existing 400,000 cap.
The payload and 196 coordinate checks require at most 60,782 new linear
units. The complete invoice must also include retained reconstruction,
Source, bootstrap, first and closing reads and authority documents.
Do not reset any production counter to run the second side. Full calls to
the old carrier checker on both maximum carriers would exceed the 200,000
linear cap, which is why those calls are omitted from this certificate.

The existing faithful Original frame, exact quartet and case association,
current unpaid selector and whole input checks remain required. A new
consumer needs a complete Source manifest, proof, protocol, distinct review
and fresh actual controls before case use. Existing nongeneration controls
do not establish this different predicate.

Controls must cover exact extent and labels, future/cyclic parents, inverse
orientation, unequal full matrices, equality only on one vector, membership
inside D, premature/nonclosing orders, resource stops and wrong or paid
case imports. A symbolic positive fixture uses (z,a,b,z*a), with a=(12),
b=(23) and z a commuting swap on disjoint coordinates. The common element
z has words [0] and [1,3], and lies outside <a,b>.

Discovery, final word verification and typed case adoption are separate.
The proposed fixed-vector heuristic for the remaining cases has not been
tested, and no named end group, normalizer or ambient order is assumed by
the word argument.
